{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29351 - PROTEIN:5488",
  "verbalization": "L-Lactic acid is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the activation of EW-22 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that L-Lactic acid acts as a target for multiple compounds, including D-423MG and 2-Chloro-5-Methoxy-3-Methylcyclohexa-2,5-Diene-1,4-Dione, which in turn target EW-22. This indicates that L-Lactic acid may serve as a common intermediate or substrate in the metabolic or signaling pathways that ultimately lead to the activation of EW-22. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting EW-22, all of which share a common target D-423MG, suggests a potential mechanism involving the metabolic transformation of L-Lactic acid into a more active form that interacts with EW-22. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility of a broader biological role for L-Lactic acid in modulating the activity of EW-22 through a series of interconnected molecular events.",
